      "title": "Robotheca: an open catalogue of 475 buildable open-source robots, with ROS 2 support, URDFs and licences checked",
      "link": "https://discourse.openrobotics.org/t/robotheca-an-open-catalogue-of-475-buildable-open-source-robots-with-ros-2-support-urdfs-and-licences-checked/59166",
      "summary": "Hi all, I’m Klajdi. I’ve been building Robotheca , a free catalogue of open-source robots you can actually build, and the software around them. It’s still in beta, and before going further I’d love to hear from people who build robots for real. What’s there today 475 robots: arms, quadrupeds, humanoids, rovers, drones… 800+ robotics software projects and 75+ AI models For each robot: the CAD/STL files, the parts list (with prices when the creator gives them), the hardware and software licences, the build guide and difficulty, and tags like ROS 2 or URDF Licences are read from each project’s own files. When they’re unclear, the page says “Unknown” instead of guessing Every creator is credited and linked to their own repository What I’d love to know Is this useful to you? What’s good, what’s confusing, what’s missing? Which robots or packages should be there and aren’t? What would you like to see more of: simulation-ready robots (URDF, Gazebo), ROS 2 distro support, cost comparisons, beginner build paths, datasets…? Is anything wrong on a page you know well? Every reply helps decide what I build next. Thanks! 1 post - 1 participant Read full topic",
      "publishedAt": "2026-10-25T15:26:47+00:00",
      "updatedAt": "2026-10-25T15:26:47+00:00",
      "source": "ROS2 Discourse",
      "section_hint": "로보틱스",
      "articleText": "Robotheca: an open catalogue of 475 buildable open-source robots, with ROS 2 support, URDFs and licences checked - Projects - Open Robotics Discourse Robotheca: an open catalogue of 475 buildable open-source robots, with ROS 2 support, URDFs and licences checked Projects release , ros2 Klajdi_Haka October 25, 2026, 3:26pm 1 Hi all, I’m Klajdi. I’ve been building Robotheca , a free catalogue of open-source robots you can actually build, and the software around them. It’s still in beta, and before going further I’d love to hear from people who build robots for real. What’s there today 475 robots: arms, quadrupeds, humanoids, rovers, drones… 800+ robotics software projects and 75+ AI models For each robot: the CAD/STL files, the parts list (with prices when the creator gives them), the hardware and software licences, the build guide and difficulty, and tags like ROS 2 or URDF Licences are read from each project’s own files. When they’re unclear, the page says “Unknown” instead of guessing Every creator is credited and linked to their own repository What I’d love to know Is this useful to you? What’s good, what’s confusing, what’s missing? Which robots or packages should be there and aren’t? What would you like to see more of: simulation-ready robots (URDF, Gazebo), ROS 2 distro support, cost comparisons, beginner build paths, datasets…? Is anything wrong on a page you know well? Every reply helps decide what I build next. Thanks! 1 Like Related topics Topic Replies Views Activity RoboParts — Structured Dataset & Selection Engine for Bionic Robot Components Projects 0 67 August 12, 2026 RoboStacker: describe your robot, get a ROS 2 stack and a workspace to build (feedback welcome) Projects release , ros2 1 102 October 5, 2026 Suggestions for Ready Robots that will be supported on Robolaunch Platform ROS General ros2 , simulation , kubernetes , development , cloud 10 1215 October 9, 2022 Largest ROS Example App/Robot Source Code ROS General 4 3100 April 21, 2016 Built a browser-based tool to assemble robots & export URDFs in minutes Projects ros2 , simulation , cad , urdf , robotics 1 334 September 22, 2025",
