      "title": "Introducing Kimi K3.1 Pro",
      "link": "https://simonwillison.net/2026/Oct/23/kimi-k31-pro/",
      "summary": "Introducing Kimi K3.1 Pro Kimi K3.1 Pro landed on the Kimi API today - it's not yet open weights, but Moonshot promise \"Full model weights will be released by Nov 4, 2026\". They're also offering a \"Highspeed\" version that's 2-3x faster, at twice the price (except for input token cache hits, which are priced the same). The US dollar pricing is $2.00/million tokens for input and $10/million for output - the same as GPT-6.1 Sol and half the price of Claude Opus 5.5. Moonshot's own benchmarks show Kimi as approximately level with Opus 5.5 and GPT-6 Astra - beating them on a few benchmarks, coming close on others. Artificial Analysis scored Kimi at 55 - ahead of Claude Fable 5.1, GPT-6 Astra, and Gemini 4 Argon (all at 53) and behind only Claude Opus 5.5 (58). This is the first time a (soon-to-be) open weight model has scored this highly against the frontier. I tried it out via the Moonshot API using the llm openai endpoint command I added to LLM 0.32 back in August: llm openai endpoint \\ https://api.moonshot.ai/v1 \\ --key kimi \\ -m kimi-k3.1-pro \\ \"Generate an SVG of a pelican riding a bicycle\" \\ --responses \\ -o reasoning_effort low \\ > kimi-k3.1-pro-pelican-low.stdout.txt \\ 2> kimi-k",
      "publishedAt": "2026-10-23T19:40:54+00:00",
      "updatedAt": "2026-10-23T19:40:54+00:00",
      "source": "Simon Willison",
      "section_hint": "AI",
      "articleText": "Introducing Kimi K3.1 Pro Simon Willison’s Weblog Newsletter Sponsored by: WorkOS Airlock — intent-based access control for AI agents. Request early access 23rd October 2026 - Link Blog Introducing Kimi K3.1 Pro (via ) Kimi K3.1 Pro landed on the Kimi API today - it's not yet open weights, but Moonshot promise \"Full model weights will be released by Nov 4, 2026\". They're also offering a \"Highspeed\" version that's 2-3x faster, at twice the price (except for input token cache hits, which are priced the same). The US dollar pricing is $2.00/million tokens for input and $10/million for output - the same as GPT-6.1 Sol and half the price of Claude Opus 5.5. Moonshot's own benchmarks show Kimi as approximately level with Opus 5.5 and GPT-6 Astra - beating them on a few benchmarks, coming close on others. Artificial Analysis scored Kimi at 55 - ahead of Claude Fable 5.1, GPT-6 Astra, and Gemini 4 Argon (all at 53) and behind only Claude Opus 5.5 (58). This is the first time a (soon-to-be) open weight model has scored this highly against the frontier. I tried it out via the Moonshot API using the llm openai endpoint command I added to LLM 0.32 back in August: llm openai endpoint \\ https://api.moonshot.ai/v1 \\ --key kimi \\ -m kimi-k3.1-pro \\ \"Generate an SVG of a pelican riding a bicycle\" \\ --responses \\ -o reasoning_effort low \\ > kimi-k3.1-pro-pelican-low.stdout.txt \\ 2> kimi-k3.1-pro-pelican-low.stderr.txt llm openai endpoint can run prompts against any OpenAI-compatible endpoint but doesn't log the results, hence the extra options to save stdout and stderr (the reasoning trace). Here are the pelicans I got for Kimi K3.1 Pro on the three reasoning levels it supports - low, medium, and max. This is max: For comparison, I ran fresh pelicans against Kimi K3 on those three reasoning levels. Posted 23rd October 2026 at 7:40 pm Recent articles Battle Drones - a vibe coded RTS with audio-based multiplayer - 20th October 2026 Hello Python 3.15, goodbye 3.10, and now I can use 3.11 - 12th October 2026 A new feature for my blog, built using my voice - 9th October 2026 Claude Haiku 5.5 - 7th October 2026 This is a link post by Simon Willison, posted on 23rd October 2026 . ai 2,293 generative-ai 2,034 llms 1,999 llm 642 llm-pricing 94 pelican-riding-a-bicycle 154 llm-release 238 ai-in-china 110 moonshot 10 kimi 14 Monthly briefing Sponsor me for $10/month and get a curated email digest of the month's most important LLM developments. Pay me to send you less! Sponsor & subscribe Disclosures Colophon © 2002 2003 2004 2005 2006 2007 2008 2009 2010 2011 2012 2013 2014 2015 2016 2017 2018 2019 2020 2021 2022 2023 2024 2025 2026",
