    {
      "title": "MCP Servers v2.1.0",
      "link": "https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/servers/releases/tag/v2.1.0",
      "summary": "Security fixes v2.1.0 fixes eight vulnerabilities in three servers. Upgrade @modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem and @modelcontextprotocol/server-everything to 2.0.1, and mcp-server-fetch to 2026.10.24. Package Affected Fixed in @modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem 1.0.0 through 2.0.0, and date versions through 2026.8.31 2.0.1 @modelcontextprotocol/server-everything 1.0.0 through 2.0.0, and date versions 2025.9.24 through 2026.8.31 2.0.1 mcp-server-fetch through 2026.10.19 2026.10.24 @modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem 2.0.1 Writes stay inside the directory that was checked (Linux and macOS). A parent directory swapped for a symlink between the access check and the write can no longer redirect write_file , edit_file , create_directory or the move_file destination outside the allowed directories. On Windows this is only partly fixed ; the advisory says what is still exposed and how to configure around it (GHSA-53mr-w429-c597 ) Paths are checked exactly as they are used. The access check no longer strips a trailing quote or whitespace that the file operation keeps, so a sibling directory named after an allowed one with that suffix is no longer reachable (GHSA-7rgq-gccq-qphx",
      "source": "GitHub (MCP Servers)",
      "updatedAt": "2026-10-25T00:03:20+00:00",
      "releaseTag": "v2.1.0",
      "isPrerelease": false,
      "section_hint": "AI",
      "articleText": "## Security fixes\r\n\r\nv2.1.0 fixes eight vulnerabilities in three servers. Upgrade\r\n`@modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem` and `@modelcontextprotocol/server-everything`\r\nto 2.0.1, and `mcp-server-fetch` to 2026.10.24.\r\n\r\n| Package | Affected | Fixed in |\r\n| --- | --- | --- |\r\n| `@modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem` | 1.0.0 through 2.0.0, and date versions through 2026.8.31 | 2.0.1 |\r\n| `@modelcontextprotocol/server-everything` | 1.0.0 through 2.0.0, and date versions 2025.9.24 through 2026.8.31 | 2.0.1 |\r\n| `mcp-server-fetch` | through 2026.10.19 | 2026.10.24 |\r\n\r\n### `@modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem` 2.0.1\r\n\r\n* **Writes stay inside the directory that was checked** (Linux and macOS). A parent directory swapped for a symlink between the access check and the write can no longer redirect `write_file`, `edit_file`, `create_directory` or the `move_file` destination outside the allowed directories. **On Windows this is only partly fixed**; the advisory says what is still exposed and how to configure around it ([GHSA-53mr-w429-c597](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/servers/security/advisories/GHSA-53mr-w429-c597))\r\n* **Paths are checked exactly as they are used.** The access check no longer strips a trailing quote or whitespace that the file operation keeps, so a sibling directory named after an allowed one with that suffix is no longer reachable ([GHSA-7rgq-gccq-qphx](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/servers/security/advisories/GHSA-7rgq-gccq-qphx))\r\n* **A symlink spelled in a different letter case no longer passes the symlink check** for a new path on a case-insensitive volume, such as macOS's default. This was a regression in 2026.8.31 ([GHSA-4gxg-m5jx-9j57](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/servers/security/advisories/GHSA-4gxg-m5jx-9j57))\r\n* **`list_directory_with_sizes` checks each entry before reading its size**, so a symlink inside an allowed directory no longer reveals the size and modification time of a file outside it ([GHSA-hhwq-wxfx-cj7g](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/servers/security/advisories/GHSA-hhwq-wxfx-cj7g))\r\n\r\n### `@modelcontextprotocol/server-everything` 2.0.1\r\n\r\n* **The HTTP and SSE transports refuse requests from other web origins.** They now check the `Origin` header and no longer send `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *`, so a web page the user visits can no longer call the server's tools (such as `get-env`) or read their results ([GHSA-mvf5-2qqv-rg3c](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/servers/security/advisories/GHSA-mvf5-2qqv-rg3c))\r\n\r\n### `mcp-server-fetch` 2026.10.24\r\n\r\n* **The address check and the connection use the same host name.** For an internationalized (IDNA) host name, the server used to check one form of the name and connect to another, which could reach an internal address ([GHSA-v38p-wf49-hx2j](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/servers/security/advisories/GHSA-v38p-wf49-hx2j))\r\n* **NAT64 addresses are judged by the IPv4 address they carry.** An address in `64:ff9b::/96` that wraps a private, loopback or link-local IPv4 address is now refused, as an IPv4-mapped one already was ([GHSA-66qx-2266-pmj6](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/servers/security/advisories/GHSA-66qx-2266-pmj6))\r\n* **robots.txt is checked again after every redirect**, not only for the URL first requested ([GHSA-3jqg-r5pp-rmp2](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/servers/security/advisories/GHSA-3jqg-r5pp-rmp2))\r\n\r\n### Upgrading from a date-versioned npm release\r\n\r\nThe TypeScript servers moved from date versions (2025.x, 2026.x) to semantic versions in 1.0.0. Package managers rank 2.0.1 below every 2025.x and 2026.x version, so they won't offer it as an upgrade. If you are on a date version, install 2.0.1 explicitly, for example `npm install @modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem@2.0.1`.\r\n\r\n## Packages\r\n\r\n| Package | Version | Registry | In this release |\r\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\r\n| `@modelcontextprotocol/server-everything` | `2.0.1` | npm | **published** |\r\n| `@modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem` | `2.0.1` | npm | **published** |\r\n| `@modelcontextprotocol/server-memory` | `2.0.0` | npm | unchanged |\r\n| `@modelcontextprotocol/server-sequential-thinking` | `2.0.0` | npm | unchanged |\r\n| `mcp-server-fetch` | `2026.10.24` | PyPI | **published** |\r\n| `mcp-server-git` | `2026.10.19` | PyPI | unchanged |\r\n| `mcp-server-time` | `2026.10.19` | PyPI | unchanged |\r\n\r\nRelease ledger: [v2/chore/5243-release-v2.1.0](https://claude.ai/artifact/KRKhZfRxCMpwsUBSyPw1n3)\r\n\r\n## @modelcontextprotocol/server-everything 2.0.1\r\n\r\n### What's Changed\r\n\r\n* fix(everything): harden HTTP transport request handling by @cliffhall in https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/servers/pull/5241\r\n* chore(deps): v2.1.0 release audit fixes by @cliffhall in https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/servers/pull/5247\r\n* chore: version packages by @github-actions[bot] in https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/servers/pull/5242\r\n* Release v2.1.0: merge v2/main into main by @cliffhall in https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/servers/pull/5249\r\n\r\n## @modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem 2.0.1\r\n\r\n### What's Changed\r\n\r\n* fix(filesystem): harden path handling for new paths by @cliffhall in https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/servers/pull/5236\r\n* fix(filesystem): harden path handling in write operations by @cliffhall in https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/servers/pull/5237\r\n* fix(filesystem): harden path handling in directory listings by @cliffhall in https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/servers/pull/5234\r\n* fix(filesystem): harden path handling by @cliffhall in https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/servers/pull/5235\r\n* chore(deps): v2.1.0 release audit fixes by @cliffhall in https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/servers/pull/5247\r\n* chore: version packages by @github-actions[bot] in https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/servers/pull/5242\r\n* Release v2.1.0: merge v2/main into main by @cliffhall in https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/servers/pull/5249\r\n\r\n## mcp-server-fetch 2026.10.24\r\n\r\n### What's Changed\r\n\r\n* fix(fetch): harden address classification by @cliffhall in https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/servers/pull/5238\r\n* fix(fetch): harden robots.txt handling by @cliffhall in https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/servers/pull/5239\r\n* fix(fetch): check the host name the connection uses by @cliffhall in https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/servers/pull/5240\r\n* chore(fetch): bump certifi to 2026.10.19 in uv.lock (GHSA-6q48-6c7w-9gw2) by @cliffhall in https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/servers/pull/5244\r\n* chore: stamp Python CalVer versions for 2026.10.24 by @github-actions[bot] in https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/servers/pull/5248\r\n* Release v2.1.0: merge v2/main into main by @cliffhall in https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/servers/pull/5249\r\n\r\n## Repository\r\n\r\n### What's Changed\r\n\r\n* docs: all work in a fresh worktree, with the session started inside it by @cliffhall in https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/servers/pull/5219\r\n* docs(skills): keep argument placeholders out of skill bodies by @cliffhall in https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/servers/pull/5220\r\n* ci: dispatch DCO and the Everything diff on version PRs opened by automation by @cliffhall in https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/servers/pull/5222\r\n* docs: link the Version Packages PR to its release issue, not only by comment by @cliffhall in https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/servers/pull/5221\r\n* docs(skills): add the advisory follow-up draft card convention by @cliffhall in https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/servers/pull/5233\r\n* chore(deps): upgrade the MCP TypeScript SDK to 2.4.0 and the Node.js adapter to 2.1.2 by @cliffhall in https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/servers/pull/5245\r\n* test(memory): accept either EISDIR message form, whatever the platform by @cliffhall in https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/servers/pull/5246\r\n\r\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/servers/compare/v2.0.0...v2.1.0\r\n\r\n## Thanks for helping us improve\r\n\r\nThis release addresses vulnerabilities reported by these community members. Thank you for taking the time to report them:\r\n\r\n* @0xCoDSnet (GHSA-4gxg-m5jx-9j57, GHSA-3jqg-r5pp-rmp2)\r\n* @cybercraftsolutionsllc (GHSA-hhwq-wxfx-cj7g)\r\n* @dizconnectz (GHSA-v38p-wf49-hx2j)\r\n* @ehudmelzer (GHSA-mvf5-2qqv-rg3c)\r\n* @golang-not-rust (GHSA-53mr-w429-c597)\r\n* @HunterX461 (GHSA-7rgq-gccq-qphx)\r\n* @LeonMAG (GHSA-66qx-2266-pmj6)\r\n* @pacocartones (GHSA-66qx-2266-pmj6)\r\n\r\nAnd to this contributor, whose prototyped fix ships in this release:\r\n\r\n* @ace-ify, the platform-independent EISDIR assertion for #5162, shipped as #5246\r\n",
      "articleUrl": "https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/servers/releases/tags/v2.1.0",
