      "title": "RoboStack moved to a Monorepo",
      "link": "https://discourse.openrobotics.org/t/robostack-moved-to-a-monorepo/59196",
      "summary": "Hi everyone, RoboStack has moved to a monorepo approach! You can read all about it in this document . Why? All the major distros are now managed from one repo. This removes a lot of duplication and makes maintaining the distro channels much easier. Patches, new packages, testing and rebuilds can now be done for all distros at once, in a single PR. Easier to contribute We added several features to help new maintainers get started. The biggest one is the new robostack-bot . It takes care of some of the regular maintenance work and can generate PR’s for standardized functions like adding a new package. You can ask it for help by commenting @robostack-bot add-package <pkg>... [<distro>...] on GitHub. Is your package already there? Check the package lists, for example for Lyrical: ROS 2 Lyrical | RoboStack If something is missing, open an issue and the bot can help get it added. Feedback and new contributors are very welcome! 1 post - 1 participant Read full topic",
      "publishedAt": "2026-10-26T10:10:44+00:00",
      "updatedAt": "2026-10-26T10:10:44+00:00",
      "source": "ROS2 Discourse",
      "section_hint": "로보틱스",
      "articleText": "RoboStack moved to a Monorepo - Mirrors - Open Robotics Discourse RoboStack moved to a Monorepo Infrastructure Project Mirrors ruben-arts October 26, 2026, 10:10am 1 Hi everyone, RoboStack has moved to a monorepo approach! You can read all about it in this document . Why? All the major distros are now managed from one repo. This removes a lot of duplication and makes maintaining the distro channels much easier. Patches, new packages, testing and rebuilds can now be done for all distros at once, in a single PR. Easier to contribute We added several features to help new maintainers get started. The biggest one is the new robostack-bot . It takes care of some of the regular maintenance work and can generate PR’s for standardized functions like adding a new package. You can ask it for help by commenting @robostack-bot add-package <pkg>... [<distro>...] on GitHub. Is your package already there? Check the package lists, for example for Lyrical: ROS 2 Lyrical | RoboStack If something is missing, open an issue and the bot can help get it added. Feedback and new contributors are very welcome! 5 Likes Related topics Topic Replies Views Activity Best practice on maintaining a repository Projects 6 3887 July 15, 2017 Invité ROSConFr 2022 Francophone Users Group 0 484 March 24, 2022 Migration to one GitHub repo for MoveIt! Manipulation 38 9654 August 16, 2018 Releasing repositories form \"other\" people Packaging and Release Management 19 5326 February 10, 2018 New way of installing ROS ROS General 7 1680 October 6, 2023",
