      "title": "BTick — Behavior Tree Monitoring & Debugging for ROS 2",
      "link": "https://discourse.openrobotics.org/t/btick-behavior-tree-monitoring-debugging-for-ros-2/59220",
      "summary": "Hi ROS community! Working with Behavior Trees in robotics? Meet BTick, a powerful tool designed to make monitoring, debugging, and analyzing BehaviorTree.CPP applications easier and more interactive. Key Features Unlimited Nodes & Multi-Tree Support — Automatically discover and monitor multiple trees and nested subtrees in real time. Live Monitoring & Interactive Debugging — Track execution, use breakpoints and step execution, and inspect node states. Runtime Control & Testing — Override node statuses, inject delays, edit supported ports, and inspect or modify Blackboard variables. Recording, Replay & Performance Analysis — Record sessions, replay execution through a timeline, export logs, and analyze execution timing. Integrated XML Editor — Create and edit BehaviorTree.CPP v4 XML files with interactive visualization and navigation. Three Protocols & Integrations BTick Protocol — Native monitoring and interactive debugging. Groot2 Protocol — Groot2-compatible communication and supported Pro features. Nav2 Integration — Visualize Behavior Trees through the ROS 2 Nav2 logging topic. Web & Desktop Applications — Access BTick through a browser or a standalone desktop application. Expl",
      "publishedAt": "2026-10-26T15:08:44+00:00",
      "updatedAt": "2026-10-26T15:08:44+00:00",
      "source": "ROS2 Discourse",
      "section_hint": "로보틱스",
      "articleText": "BTick — Behavior Tree Monitoring & Debugging for ROS 2 - Projects - Open Robotics Discourse BTick — Behavior Tree Monitoring & Debugging for ROS 2 Projects ros2 , nav2 , behaviortrees Sherif_Fathey October 26, 2026, 3:08pm 1 Hi ROS community! Working with Behavior Trees in robotics? Meet BTick, a powerful tool designed to make monitoring, debugging, and analyzing BehaviorTree.CPP applications easier and more interactive. Key Features Unlimited Nodes & Multi-Tree Support — Automatically discover and monitor multiple trees and nested subtrees in real time. Live Monitoring & Interactive Debugging — Track execution, use breakpoints and step execution, and inspect node states. Runtime Control & Testing — Override node statuses, inject delays, edit supported ports, and inspect or modify Blackboard variables. Recording, Replay & Performance Analysis — Record sessions, replay execution through a timeline, export logs, and analyze execution timing. Integrated XML Editor — Create and edit BehaviorTree.CPP v4 XML files with interactive visualization and navigation. Three Protocols & Integrations BTick Protocol — Native monitoring and interactive debugging. Groot2 Protocol — Groot2-compatible communication and supported Pro features. Nav2 Integration — Visualize Behavior Trees through the ROS 2 Nav2 logging topic. Web & Desktop Applications — Access BTick through a browser or a standalone desktop application. Explore BTick Full Demo: [Demo Link] Documentation: BTick: Behavior Tree Visualizer & Debugger — BTick 1.0.0 documentation Application Repository: GitHub - SherifFathey/btick_app · GitHub Core Integration: GitHub - SherifFathey/btick · GitHub Built for developers working with ROS 2, BehaviorTree.CPP, and Nav2. The goal is simple: bring Behavior Tree visualization, monitoring, debugging, recording, and analysis together in one interface. Feedback and contributions are welcome! Monitor 1920×1080 306 KB xml_editor 1854×1048 202 KB 2 Likes chfritz October 26, 2026, 4:51pm 2 Looks awesome! Is this only useful for development or would it also make sense for monitoring/operating deployed robots? If the latter then I think this would make for a great Transitive capability . It would help spread the word and, on the technical side, would move the UI to the cloud with a remote connection to the robot for monitoring from the web without the need for a VPN or similar. 1 Like Sherif_Fathey October 26, 2026, 5:17pm 3 BTick — Behavior Tree Monitoring & Debugging for ROS 2 Projects Looks awesome! Is this only useful for development or would it also make sense for monitoring/operating deployed robots? If the latter then I think this would make for a great Transitive capability . It would help spread the word and, on the technical side, would move the UI to the cloud with a remote connection to the robot for monitoring from the web without the need for a VPN or similar. Thanks for the suggestion! This is definitely just the beginning for BTick. On the development side, BTick allows you to modify the Behavior Tree at runtime, making debugging, testing, and experimenting with different behaviors much easier. For deployed robots, I believe it could also be valuable for remote monitoring, troubleshooting, and diagnosing unexpected behavior in real-world operation. Integrating BTick with Transitive is a great idea, and I’ll definitely explore this direction. I’d also really appreciate it if you could try BTick on one of your real-world robotics projects and share your feedback. It would be great to hear your thoughts on how well it fits into an actual robotics workflow and what improvements would make it more useful. Related topics Topic Replies Views Activity Groot1Publisher: Visualize and Monitor BehaviorTree v4 trees in Groot 1 Projects ros2 , tools , humble , deliberation 0 308 March 6, 2026 Open Class - Behavior Trees for ROS2 Training & Education ros2 0 1120 December 22, 2022 BT-Studio 0.3 available (with video) ROS General ros2