      "title": "Ollama v0.40.12",
      "link": "https://github.com/ollama/ollama/releases/tag/v0.40.12",
      "summary": "Liquid AI LFM3 LFM3 is Liquid AI's new family of small models built for local agents, tool calling, and structured output, on Liquid's new tri-hybrid architecture. The family includes: lfm3 : a 1.7B text model with a 256K-token context window lfm3-vl : adds image understanding lfm3-audio : speech recognition, translation, and text-to-speech in 18 languages lfm3-omni : text, images, and audio in one model ollama run lfm3 d1 decision models Liquid AI's d1 models now come in a 2B size, built on LFM3. d1 makes decisions about text and images, and d1-omni adds audio. ollama run d1:2b \" I was charged twice for order 4417.\" --ask \" Is this a billing issue?\" Note: lfm3 and d1 2b are supported on Apple hardware in this release. Support for Linux/Windows coming soon. What's Changed Faster prompt processing on Apple silicon for Gemma 4, Flint and Laguna models Speculative decoding now supports DFlash2 draft models on MLX Gemma 4 keeps more detail in small images ollama launch now works with OpenCode v2 Fixed tool-only assistant turns from Kimi CLI Updated MLX and llama.cpp Full Changelog : v0.40.11...v0.40.12",
      "source": "GitHub (Ollama)",
      "updatedAt": "2026-10-27T21:41:00+00:00",
      "releaseTag": "v0.40.12",
      "isPrerelease": false,
      "section_hint": "AI",
      "articleText": "## Liquid AI LFM3\r\n\r\n[LFM3](https://ollama.com/library/lfm3) is Liquid AI's new family of small models built for local agents, tool calling, and structured output, on Liquid's new tri-hybrid architecture. The family includes:\r\n\r\n- [lfm3](https://ollama.com/library/lfm3): a 1.7B text model with a 256K-token context window\r\n- [lfm3-vl](https://ollama.com/library/lfm3-vl): adds image understanding\r\n- [lfm3-audio](https://ollama.com/library/lfm3-audio): speech recognition, translation, and text-to-speech in 18 languages\r\n- [lfm3-omni](https://ollama.com/library/lfm3-omni): text, images, and audio in one model\r\n\r\n```sh\r\nollama run lfm3\r\n```\r\n\r\n## d1 decision models\r\n\r\nLiquid AI's d1 models now come in a 2B size, built on LFM3. [d1](https://ollama.com/library/d1) makes decisions about text and images, and [d1-omni](https://ollama.com/library/d1-omni) adds audio.\r\n\r\n```sh\r\nollama run d1:2b \"I was charged twice for order 4417.\" --ask \"Is this a billing issue?\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nNote: lfm3 and d1 2b are supported on Apple hardware in this release.  Support for Linux/Windows coming soon.\r\n\r\n## What's Changed\r\n- Faster prompt processing on Apple silicon for Gemma 4, Flint and Laguna models\r\n- Speculative decoding now supports DFlash2 draft models on MLX\r\n- Gemma 4 keeps more detail in small images\r\n- `ollama launch` now works with OpenCode v2\r\n- Fixed tool-only assistant turns from Kimi CLI\r\n- Updated MLX and llama.cpp\r\n\r\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/ollama/ollama/compare/v0.40.11...v0.40.12",
