      "title": "[STVL] New Obstruction Zones!",
      "link": "https://discourse.openrobotics.org/t/stvl-new-obstruction-zones/59298",
      "summary": "Howdy everyone - your friendly neighborhood navigator here! I wanted to let you know quickly about a new feature in STVL that I think is very useful for the community - Obstruction Zones ! Courtesy of Remco , these allow you to specify occlusions to your sensors to treat them specially in the decay functions so that they remain present when in-bounds of the sensor frustum so they aren’t actively decayed. STVL was originally designed with high-visibility sensor configurations in mind (8+ RGBD cameras; top mounted 3D lidar) so this is a wonderful addition for those with dead areas in the sensor FOV due to self-collision or similar. Pull request SteveMacenski/spatio_temporal_voxel_layer [ros2] added obstruction polygons to 3d lidar frustrum (#367) ros2 ← remco-r:feature/ros2_obstruction_polygons remco-r opened 08:22PM - 21 Oct 26 UTC +687 -12 ## Add FOV Obstruction Polygons for 3D Lidar Frustum I introduced the option … to add \"obstruction polygons\" to the 3D lidar frustum. This way obstructions which are part of the robot body are considered out of field of view and persist accordingly. <img width=\"400\" height=\"319\" alt=\"stvl_forklift_2x\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/asse",
      "publishedAt": "2026-10-28T18:37:15+00:00",
      "updatedAt": "2026-10-28T18:37:15+00:00",
      "source": "ROS2 Discourse",
      "section_hint": "로보틱스",
      "articleText": "[ros2] added obstruction polygons to 3d lidar frustrum (#367) ros2 ← remco-r:feature/ros2_obstruction_polygons remco-r opened 08:22PM - 21 Oct 26 UTC +687 -12 ## Add FOV Obstruction Polygons for 3D Lidar Frustum I introduced the option … to add \"obstruction polygons\" to the 3D lidar frustum. This way obstructions which are part of the robot body are considered out of field of view and persist accordingly. <img width=\"400\" height=\"319\" alt=\"stvl_forklift_2x\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b23ec4bd-3936-412c-9d30-72afe4208656\" /> _Orange voxels (new) are persisted as they are behind obstruction polygons._ This is the `ros2` targeted PR of https://github.com/SteveMacenski/spatio_temporal_voxel_layer/pull/357 TODO: - [x] rebase from jazzy - [x] pass build in ros2 lyrical - [x] verify correct obstruction filtering / no regressions - [x] handle 4407b6a \"support asymmetric lidar\"",
      "articleUrl": "https://discourse.openrobotics.org/t/stvl-new-obstruction-zones/59298",
