      "title": "ROS 2 GUI Installer – Making ROS 2 Setup Easier for Beginners",
      "link": "https://discourse.openrobotics.org/t/ros-2-gui-installer-making-ros-2-setup-easier-for-beginners/59289",
      "summary": "Hey everyone! We recently open-sourced ROS 2 GUI Installer , a tool we developed at RUNTIME Robotics to simplify ROS 2 installation, especially for absolute beginners. It provides a simple GUI to install ROS 2, Gazebo, Nav2, MoveIt 2, and other commonly used packages. One feature I find particularly useful is Workshop Profiles . You can create a YAML profile with the packages and configurations needed for a workshop and share it with participants so they can easily replicate the setup on their machines. It currently supports ROS 2 Humble, Jazzy, and Lyrical. GitHub - runtimerobotics/ros2_gui_installer: Beginner-friendly GTK4 GUI installer for ROS 2 (Humble, Jazzy, Lyrical): base, simulation, mobile robot, Nav2, arm, MoveIt 2 · GitHub Hope this is useful to the community! Would love to hear your feedback and suggestions. 3 posts - 2 participants Read full topic",
      "publishedAt": "2026-10-28T14:30:30+00:00",
      "updatedAt": "2026-10-28T14:30:30+00:00",
      "source": "ROS2 Discourse",
      "section_hint": "로보틱스",
      "articleText": "ROS 2 GUI Installer – Making ROS 2 Setup Easier for Beginners - Training & Education - Open Robotics Discourse ROS 2 GUI Installer – Making ROS 2 Setup Easier for Beginners Training & Education ros2 , gazebo , education , training lentinjoseph October 28, 2026, 2:30pm 1 Hey everyone! We recently open-sourced ROS 2 GUI Installer , a tool we developed at RUNTIME Robotics to simplify ROS 2 installation, especially for absolute beginners. ROS 2 GUI Installer Footer Update 1122×1402 329 KB It provides a simple GUI to install ROS 2, Gazebo, Nav2, MoveIt 2, and other commonly used packages. One feature I find particularly useful is Workshop Profiles . You can create a YAML profile with the packages and configurations needed for a workshop and share it with participants so they can easily replicate the setup on their machines. It currently supports ROS 2 Humble, Jazzy, and Lyrical. GitHub - runtimerobotics/ros2_gui_installer: Beginner-friendly GTK4 GUI installer for ROS 2 (Humble, Jazzy, Lyrical): base, simulation, mobile robot, Nav2, arm, MoveIt 2 · GitHub Hope this is useful to the community! Would love to hear your feedback and suggestions. 1 Like charlotteevans October 28, 2026, 6:08pm 2 The Workshop Profiles idea seems like the most practical part of this, since getting everyone in a room onto the same package set is usually where a lot of time disappears. I am curious how much the profiles lock down beyond package selection, for example whether they can pin specific versions or leave room for local variations. The three-distro support for Humble, Jazzy, and Lyrical also feels considered rather than just chasing the newest release. Denver has a decent meetup scene, and something like this could make introductory sessions less about troubleshooting installs. 1 Like lentinjoseph October 28, 2026, 8:53pm 3 Thanks! A profile sets the ROS 2 version, the ROS install type, categories, extra packages and network settings (domain ID, middleware, localhost-only). It doesn’t pin package versions: everyone gets the current release from the ROS apt repo, so a room installing on the same day ends up matching. It leaves room for local variation, because the profile only pre-ticks choices and each person can add more before pressing Install. A profile targets one distro, and Humble, Jazzy and Lyrical are all supported, so a workshop can stay on an LTS. Would love to hear how it goes at a Denver meetup! Related topics Topic Replies Views Activity ROS 2 Robot V1.0.0 - A Modern GUI for ROS 2 Workspace Management (Like GitHub Desktop for ROS) ROS General release , ros2 , automate , gui 1 357 June 18, 2026 Learning ROS 2 Basics Training & Education ros2 0 728 August 15, 2022 Tutorial: ICRA 2023 ROS 2 and new Gazebo Tutorial materials ROS General ros2 , gazebo , tutorial 0 1907 July 23, 2023 Visual IDE for Teaching ROS 2 on Windows (Early MVP, Feedback Welcome) Projects 4 250 January 10, 2026 Need help with a library for which makes using ROS 2 easier Projects 3 711 March 1, 2023",
      "articleUrl": "https://discourse.openrobotics.org/t/ros-2-gui-installer-making-ros-2-setup-easier-for-beginners/59289",
      "articleFetchedAt": "2026-10-29T00:29:25.429758+00:00",
