      "source": "Simon Willison",
      "section_hint": "AI",
      "articleText": "A quote from Terk Terkowitz Simon Willison’s Weblog Newsletter Sponsored by: WorkOS Airlock — intent-based access control for AI agents. Request early access 28th October 2026 If your work does not benefit from current AI tooling, that is a finding, not a failing. Document why, share it with your community of peers, bring it to your manager, and work to find solutions. An engineer who can explain where AI does not yet help their work is demonstrating the judgement we are asking for. — Terk Terkowitz , An update from Amazon engineering leadership on the role of the developer in the age of AI Posted 28th October 2026 at 10:09 am Recent articles The October inflection point for vibe game development - 28th October 2026 Battle Drones - a vibe coded RTS with audio-based multiplayer - 20th October 2026 Hello Python 3.15, goodbye 3.10, and now I can use 3.11 - 12th October 2026 A new feature for my blog, built using my voice - 9th October 2026 This is a quotation collected by Simon Willison, posted on 28th October 2026 . amazon 71 ai 2,300 generative-ai 2,041 llms 2,006 agentic-engineering 69 Disclosures Colophon © 2002 2003 2004 2005 2006 2007 2008 2009 2010 2011 2012 2013 2014 2015 2016 2017 2018 2019 2020 2021 2022 2023 2024 2025 2026",
