      "summary": "Verify Docker Image Signature All LiteLLM Docker images are signed with cosign . This release is signed with the key introduced in commit e82a3c6 . Verify using the pinned commit hash (recommended): A commit hash is cryptographically immutable, so this is the strongest way to ensure you are using the published signing key: cosign verify \\ --key https://raw.githubusercontent.com/BerriAI/litellm/e82a3c646908ba0a6ee0beddc4310d7a6cac4065/cosign.pub \\ ghcr.io/berriai/litellm:v1.106.6 Verify using the release tag (convenience): Tags are protected in this repository and resolve to the same key. This option is easier to read but relies on tag protection rules: cosign verify \\ --key https://raw.githubusercontent.com/BerriAI/litellm/v1.106.6/cosign.pub \\ ghcr.io/berriai/litellm:v1.106.6 Expected output: The following checks were performed on each of these signatures: - The cosign claims were validated - The signatures were verified against the specified public key What's Changed fix(proxy): backport #46712 gzip scoping and off-loop compression to stable/1.106.x for v1.106.6 by @kerry-berri in #48680 Full Changelog : v1.106.5...v1.106.6",
