      "title": "Dedicated meeting to discuss REP 0157: Wednesday, 4 November 2026",
      "link": "https://discourse.openrobotics.org/t/dedicated-meeting-to-discuss-rep-0157-wednesday-4-november-2026/59331",
      "summary": "Dedicated meeting to discuss REP 0157: Wednesday, 4 November 2026 Hi everyone, At the ROS 2 PMC meeting on 27 October 2026 we discussed REP 0157 . There is a lot to cover, so the PMC agreed to hold a dedicated meeting on this REP. Anyone interested in REP 0157 is welcome to join. What is REP 0157? REP 0157 redesigns the rosidl messaging system so that ROS 2 gets native, universal zero-copy transport across process boundaries with minimal overhead. Key features: language-agnostic memory layouts, strict message constraints, and standardizing on XCDRv1 as the in-memory representation. Compatibility: designed to be backward compatible, with support for C, C++ and Python . Implementation: groups such as Ekumen-OS maintain experimental reference implementations and benchmarks to test constrained publisher and subscriber loans. When Wednesday, 4 November 2026 at 9:30 AM PST (17:30 UTC) Your local time: Wed, Nov 4, 2026 5:30 PM UTC Note: US daylight saving time ends on 1 November, so the meeting is at 9:30 PST (UTC-8). Where Meeting link: Google Meet meeting Background material Please review these before the meeting so we can make the most of the time: REP 0157 draft: reps/_posts/rep-0157:",
      "publishedAt": "2026-10-29T14:45:09+00:00",
      "updatedAt": "2026-10-29T14:45:09+00:00",
