      "articleText": "Dedicated meeting to discuss REP 0157: Wednesday, 4 November 2026 - Projects - Open Robotics Discourse Dedicated meeting to discuss REP 0157: Wednesday, 4 November 2026 Projects ahcorde October 29, 2026, 2:45pm 1 Dedicated meeting to discuss REP 0157: Wednesday, 4 November 2026 Hi everyone, At the ROS 2 PMC meeting on 27 October 2026 we discussed REP 0157 . There is a lot to cover, so the PMC agreed to hold a dedicated meeting on this REP. Anyone interested in REP 0157 is welcome to join. What is REP 0157? REP 0157 redesigns the rosidl messaging system so that ROS 2 gets native, universal zero-copy transport across process boundaries with minimal overhead. Key features: language-agnostic memory layouts, strict message constraints, and standardizing on XCDRv1 as the in-memory representation. Compatibility: designed to be backward compatible, with support for C, C++ and Python . Implementation: groups such as Ekumen-OS maintain experimental reference implementations and benchmarks to test constrained publisher and subscriber loans. When Wednesday, 4 November 2026 at 9:30 AM PST (17:30 UTC) Your local time: 2026-11-04T17:30:00Z Note: US daylight saving time ends on 1 November, so the meeting is at 9:30 PST (UTC-8). Where Meeting link: Google Meet meeting Background material Please review these before the meeting so we can make the most of the time: REP 0157 draft: reps/_posts/rep-0157:2026.md at main · openrobotics/reps · GitHub ROSCon 2026 talk: Breaking through the zero-copy bottleneck with REP-0157 Agenda Short overview of REP 0157: goals, memory layout and message constraints Open questions and feedback raised during the 27 October PMC meeting Backward compatibility and the impact on C, C++ and Python users Status of the reference implementations and benchmarks Community feedback and discussion Next steps How to contribute If you can’t attend, or you want to raise something ahead of time, please reply in this thread or comment on the draft on GitHub. We will take written feedback into account during the meeting. Notes from the meeting will be posted in this thread afterwards. See you there! 2 Likes Related topics Topic Replies Views Activity Is it time to discuss rosidl? ROS General ros2 21 2260 August 8, 2026 IPC in ros2 ROS General ros2 39 13081 March 20, 2018 ROS2 Real-time Working Group Online Meeting 2 - Aug 21st, 2019 between 7AM and 8AM PDT (UTC-7) ROS General wg-real-time 23 3592 October 2, 2019 Announcing protoros2: use protobuf in ros2 without compromise ROS General rclcpp , rosbag2 , protobuf , mcap 9 742 September 2, 2026 RFC: REP-2011 Evolving Message Types ROS General 3 1918 August 24, 2022",
